    "q-134550": {
      "dom_id": "question-134550",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Given that all four squares shown in the diagram are congruent, find the perimeter $p$ of square $B.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $p=$  \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $cm$",
      "worked_solution": "Since all the squares in the graph are congruent, their sides are of equal length. \n\nFrom the graph, the measure of one of the sides is $5\\,cm$, so all four sides of square $B$ have length $5\\,cm.$\n\nThe perimeter $p$ of a polygon is the sum of the measures of all its sides. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\np=4\\cdot 5=20\\,cm.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
