    "q-134596": {
      "dom_id": "question-134596",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Find the value of $x$ given that $\\beta =(2x+3)^{∘}.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $x=$  \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The angle $\\beta $ is an angle obtained after bisecting one of the interior angles of a square by a diagonal. Therefore, we must have \n\n$$\n\\beta =\\frac{{90}^{∘}}{2}={45}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\beta  & ={45}^{∘} \\\\ (2x+3)^{∘} & ={45}^{∘} \\\\ 2x+3 & =45 \\\\ 2x & =42 \\\\ x & =21.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
