    "q-134601": {
      "dom_id": "question-134601",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Given that $\\delta =(3y-15)^{∘},$ find the value of $y.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $y=$  \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Since the two bases of the trapezoid $D$ are parallel, angles $\\delta $ and $\\gamma $ in the graph are alternate interior angles and consequently, they have the same measure. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\delta  & =\\gamma ={45}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\delta  & ={45}^{∘} \\\\ (3y-15)^{∘} & ={45}^{∘} \\\\ 3y-15 & =45 \\\\ 3y & =60 \\\\ y & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
